  "evidence": [
    "Pinned twenty ordered asset initializers/finalizers and typed storage extents support genuine global Texture owners. Five original scalar pairs call out-of-line ctor/dtor; same-TU application /Ob2 instead inlines them and exceeds original spans. Move the complete ordered twenty-global block and forty lifetime annotations without rewriting methods or extending spans.",
    "Preserve historical claims and original bug-for-bug semantics. Existing method/raster bodies, associated storage, static lookup helpers and headers remain unchanged. Source ownership grouping is not proof of historical TU boundaries. Native annotation writers alone may update emitted symbol facts and claims.",
    "Authorize only evidence-backed /Ob2 comparison recipe for the new object owner if controls establish the actual application policy reproduces its genuine complete callbacks, as for Sprite/Caviar object owners; do not change global/default flags or Texture method recipes. No future matches presumed.",
    "Require fresh build/link, paired Texture body measurements, complete original identity/claim continuity, physical callback/object correspondence and startup-order review, and relevant source tests. Outside-TU byte/linked changes remain explicit obligations. Coordinator manual integration only after review; no automatic/full-game acceptance claimed."
  ],
  "intent": "Separate application Texture asset objects and their compiler-owned lifetime mappings from Texture methods; preserve original behavior, ordering and all obligations.",
